{
  "source_commit": "9a4633df061b1b33df49772c15190d484dd207b6",
  "harness_commit": "this commit (WS4 phase 1: .native_catalog main backend)",
  "measurement_scope": "Lite write-amplification counting harness (zig build lite-write-amplification, Debug), re-run after WS4 phase 1: a .native_catalog MainBackend for PersistentIndex (storage/native_catalog_backend.zig + lite/native_catalog_sink.zig), selected by lite/backend.zig for Lite's full-text main backend (segment ranges, active segment set, generation metadata, and small segments themselves), replacing the embedded LSM instance stored through lite/index_storage.zig's virtual filesystem. Dense/sparse/graph backends are unchanged (.lsm). Same workload as the baseline and attributed receipts: 128 single-doc updates, 1 KiB changing text per update, primary_only deletes the default full_text_index_v0 index, indexed/indexed_8_writers keep it and use sync_level=full_index. Measured on perf/lwa-ws4-indexed-commit, after merging perf/lwa-integration at ca8c5eed8d (WS1 native commit protocol, WS5 retirement off the ack path, WS6 progress v2, WS7 demand-gated runtimes).",
  "comparison": {
    "indexed_calling_thread_syncs_per_update": {
      "original_pre_ws_work_baseline": 66.84375,
      "after_ws1_ws5_ws7_before_ws4": 34.5625,
      "after_ws4_native_catalog": 6.21875
    },
    "indexed_calling_thread_bytes_per_update": {
      "after_ws1_ws5_ws7_before_ws4": 423645.6640625,
      "after_ws4_native_catalog": 101141.125
    },
    "note": "original_pre_ws_work_baseline is write-amplification-baseline.json's number (measured before WS1/WS5/WS6/WS7 landed). after_ws1_ws5_ws7_before_ws4 is write-amplification-attributed.json's number, measured on this same branch before the native_catalog backend existed -- the correct 'before' for WS4's own contribution (66.8->34.6 is WS1/WS5/WS7's doing, not WS4's). after_ws4_native_catalog isolates WS4's own effect: indexed_syncs 34.6->6.2 (-82%), indexed_bytes 423.6KB->101.1KB (-76%)."
  },
  "known_limitations": [
    "Segments of every size are stored inline as native-catalog records for .native_catalog (segment_files is unconditionally null for that backend); the design doc's artifact_inline_limit (~256 KiB) split -- bounded unlinked staging + putIndexCatalogRecordFromFile for large artifacts, with a lease only when a cross-process mmap source is actually requested -- is not implemented. Harmless for this workload (1 KiB documents, small segments) but a real gap for a full-text index that accumulates large segments before merging.",
    "The projection seal (publishProjectionSeal, persistent.zig) and WS6 progress v2 (apply_state.contributeProgressTxn) are not folded into the SAME native transaction as segment+metadata: they remain separate commits, called from index_manager.zig's publishFullTextReplaySeal (WS6-owned, ~9723, not edited by this branch). Both are now cheap (also native_catalog-backed, not LSM-on-vfs), so this is a secondary, not primary, cost -- but true single-commit publication (segment + metadata + seal + progress) needs that WS6-owned call site to pass a view onto the same MainTxn this branch already opens for segment+metadata, which this branch does not do (see final report).",
    "Only one of several background/maintenance MainTxn.commit() call sites in persistent.zig (replaceSegmentsWithReservedIdOwned, the single-id merge/compaction replace path) was switched to the new setDurable(false) ride-along mechanism added in this branch. replaceSegmentsWithReservedIdsOwned (multi-id), removeSegmentsLocked, and pruneMissingActiveSegmentsLocked remain durable=true (unchanged, correct, just not yet optimized) pending a broader pass.",
    "main_txn_commit reads nonzero (284 calling-thread syncs / 128 updates = 2.2/update) for indexed mode -- not 1.0 -- because the measured workload triggers more than one publication per update at this small scale (e.g. segment build plus periodic merge/compaction); it is not evidence that one indexed write costs more than one native commit for its own direct publication."
  ],
